IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc5-s117-01-to-117-012`

-- Tests for ccc5-s117-01-to-117-012.l4. Every expected value was decided from the text before the run; a failing assertion is a finding.

-- s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1): expected values follow the text (s 117.01(4))
#ASSERT `s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to the person as the result of an order made under subsection 113(1)

-- s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order: expected values follow the text (s 117.01(1))
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: s 2 firearm: the thing possessed is one / s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1): the thing possessed is a cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition / s 2 explosive substance: the thing possessed is one
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: s 2 firearm: the thing possessed is one
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1): the thing possessed is a cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: s 2 explosive substance: the thing possessed is one
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person is prohibited from possessing it by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament
#ASSERT `s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the answer of s 117.01(4)

-- s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order: expected values follow the text (s 117.01(2))
#ASSERT `s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person wilfully fails to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer any authorization, licence or registration certificate held by the person
#ASSERT `s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person is required to do so by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament

#ASSERT `s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- no limb is made out
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a limb answered JUST FALSE is not a made-out limb
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 117.01(1) made out
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb s 117.01(2) made out

#ASSERT `s 117.01(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

#ASSERT `s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `mode` EQUALS `by indictment`
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `minimum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum fine` EQUALS `no fine is stated`

#ASSERT (`s 117.01(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`, `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 5000, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`))'s `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 117.01(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`, `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 5000, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`))'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`   -- the limb returns exactly what section 787(1) is given as
#ASSERT (`s 117.01(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`, `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 5000, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`))'s `maximum fine` EQUALS `a fine of` 5000

-- s 117.0101(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency limitations on access order: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(1))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency limitations on access order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency limitations on access order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the person against whom the order is sought cohabits with, or is an associate of, another person who is prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency limitations on access order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that the other person would or might have access to any such thing that is in the possession of the person against whom the order is sought

-- s 117.0101(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(2))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant

-- s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(3))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the provincial court judge is bound to make an emergency limitations on access order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person


-- s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days: a period stated in days; a period stated in months or years is not a period "not exceeding 30 days" (fork register)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly 30 days
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 29, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 7, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 31, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 31 days exceeds 30 days
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the period of the order is not more than 30 days` (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a month is not stated in days
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the order begins on the day on which it is made` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(3) the order begins on the day on which it is made` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 117.0101(4) a copy of the order is to be served on the person to whom it is addressed: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(4))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(4) a copy of the order is to be served on the person to whom it is addressed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(4) a copy of the order is to be served on the person to whom it is addressed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: an order has been made under subsection (3)

-- s 117.0101(5) the provincial court judge is bound to impose terms and conditions that are the least intrusive possible: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(5))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(5) the provincial court judge is bound to impose terms and conditions that are the least intrusive possible` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(5) the provincial court judge is bound to impose terms and conditions that are the least intrusive possible` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge determines terms and conditions under subsection (3)

-- s 117.0101(10) the judge may issue the warrant or include the requirement to surrender: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(10))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(10) the judge may issue the warrant or include the requirement to surrender` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(10) the judge may issue the warrant or include the requirement to surrender` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of that order can reasonably be complied with

-- s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(6))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the answer of s 117.0101(10): not settled, so the closed gate is not met
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the answer of s 117.0101(10): the text says no ("only if")

-- s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(7))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: s 2 peace officer: the officer is one
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the use and possession of which is subject to terms and conditions under the order
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (6) exist
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 peace officer: the officer is one: the other way it can fail ((JUST FALSE))

-- s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(8))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6) / the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (6)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (7)

-- s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(8))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant / the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the report is of an execution of a warrant and shows the things, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(8) the report shows what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the report is of a search without a warrant and shows the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things, if any, seized

-- s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(9))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge makes an order against the person under subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied by information on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of any person for the person to possess the thing
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the thing is in the person's possession on the day on which the order is made and its use or possession is subject to terms and conditions under the order
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the answer of s 117.0101(10): not settled, so the closed gate is not met
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the provincial court judge may require the person to surrender the things` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the answer of s 117.0101(10): the text says no ("only if")

-- s 117.0101(9) the judge is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(9))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the judge is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(9) the judge is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering the thing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge requires the person to surrender the thing

-- s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(11))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the thing has been seized under subsection (6) or (7) by the peace officer / the thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9) to the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the thing has been seized under subsection (6) or (7) by the peace officer
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the thing has been surrendered in accordance with subsection (9) to the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the person will comply with the terms and conditions of the order as to the use and possession of the thing
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING; the two where-kind limbs ("before the expiry or revocation", "on being issued a receipt") now answer JUST FALSE, and the "if the officer has reasonable grounds" limb stays NOTHING (exception: a receipt for it is issued)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 117.0101(11) the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may return the thing before the expiry or revocation of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING; the two where-kind limbs ("before the expiry or revocation", "on being issued a receipt") now answer JUST FALSE, and the "if the officer has reasonable grounds" limb stays NOTHING (exception: the order has not expired or been revoked)

-- s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person: expected values follow the text (s 117.0101(12))
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the things were seized under subsection (6) or (7) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3), or surrendered by the person in accordance with subsection (9)
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked / the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3) has ended
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3) has ended
#ASSERT `s 117.0101(12) the things are to be returned to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the things have already been returned under subsection (11)

-- s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information: expected values follow the text (s 117.0102(1))
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: an order is made under subsection 117.0101(3)
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the application is made by the person who applied for the order / the judge acts on the judge's own motion
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the application is made by the person who applied for the order
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the judge acts on the judge's own motion
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the information relates to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3) / the information relates to a warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6) / the information relates to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7) / the information relates to the order made under this subsection
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the information relates to the order made under subsection 117.0101(3)
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the information relates to a warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6)
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the information relates to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(1) the provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the information relates to the order made under this subsection


-- s 117.0102(2) the order made under subsection (1) expires on the day in question
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(2) the order made under subsection (1) expires on the day in question` (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(2) the order made under subsection (1) expires on the day in question` (Date 19 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another day: the text says only when it expires
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(2) the order made under subsection (1) expires on the day in question` (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Unless ... revoked earlier"
-- s 117.0102(3) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(3) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)   -- (a) the date fixed
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(3) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE (Date 12 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)   -- (b) revoked before that date: the day it is revoked
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(3) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no date fixed: subsection (2) governs

-- s 117.0102(4) the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge: expected values follow the text (s 117.0102(4))
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(4) the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(4) the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: an order is made under subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(4) the documents are to be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the document relates to the order made under subsection (1), the order made under subsection 117.0101(3), the warrant issued under subsection 117.0101(6) or the report made under subsection 117.0101(8)

-- s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge: expected values follow the text (s 117.0102(5))
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the application is to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order / the application is made to another provincial court judge
#ASSERT `s 117.0102(5) an application to revoke or vary the order may be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order
