#ASSERT `s 117.0104(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 117.011(1)


-- s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed
#ASSERT `s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly 15 days before: "not later than 15 days before"
#ASSERT `s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- earlier than 15 days before
#ASSERT `s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 days before is too late
#ASSERT `s 117.0104(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 16 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- on the day itself
-- the regulative rule, run (a trace prints its outcome; it cannot be asserted on the stable binary). Hearing fixed 30 days ahead: notice due by day 15.
#TRACE `s 117.0104(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 117.0104(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` AT 15
#TRACE `s 117.0104(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 117.0104(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` AT 16
#TRACE `s 117.0104(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 16

